1
00:00:00,014 --> 00:00:05,360
想象一下，你要通过短信指导某人去修复一个庞大的软件项目。
Picture trying to coach someone through fixing a sprawling software project entirely over text message.

2
00:00:05,550 --> 00:00:13,284
你可以描述该做什么，但你看不见屏幕，没法运行测试，也没法记住你三条信息前说了什么。
You can describe what to do, but you can't see the screen, you can't run the tests,
and you can't remember what you said three messages ago.

3
00:00:13,710 --> 00:00:19,748
本质上，这就是大语言模型试图作为自主智能体行动时面临的困境。
That, in essence, is the predicament of a large language model trying to act as an autonomous agent.

4
00:00:20,014 --> 00:00:25,860
而我们今天要讨论的这篇综述认为，解决这个困境的答案就在眼前。
And the survey we're walking through today argues that the answer to this predicament is hiding in plain sight.

5
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:34,480
那就是代码本身，它不是模型产出的产物，而是让模型能够行动、观察和记忆的操作脚手架。
Code itself, not as a thing the model produces, but as the operational scaffolding that lets it act, observe, and remember.

6
00:00:34,798 --> 00:00:50,560
这篇论文名为《Code as Agent Harness》，它为代码如何从语言模型的输出，
悄然演变为智能体系统实际运行的媒介，提供了一个统一的综述和概念框架。
The paper is titled Code as Agent Harness, and it offers a unified survey and conceptual framing for how code has quietly evolved from
being the output of language models into being the medium through which agentic systems actually function.

7
00:00:50,990 --> 00:01:02,450
作者借用了系统领域的术语「智能体框架（智能体框架）」，它指的是包裹语言模型的软件层，
包含工具、沙箱、内存存储、验证器、权限边界、执行循环和反馈通道。
The authors borrow a term from the systems community, the agent harness, which refers to the software layer,
wrapping a language model with tools, sandboxes, memory stores,

8
00:01:02,450 --> 00:01:07,716
作者借用了系统领域的术语「智能体框架（智能体框架）」，它指的是包裹语言模型的软件层，
包含工具、沙箱、内存存储、验证器、权限边界、执行循环和反馈通道。
validators, permission boundaries, execution loops, and feedback channels.

9
00:01:08,526 --> 00:01:21,476
他们的核心观点是，自主智能体的瓶颈不再仅仅是原始的推理能力，
而是将模型输出连接到长期行动和持久状态的智能体框架的可靠性。
Their core claim is that the bottleneck for autonomous agents is no longer just raw reasoning ability,
but the reliability of the harness that connects model outputs to long-running actions and persistent state.

10
00:01:22,222 --> 00:01:32,644
他们认为，代码是作为这种智能体框架的基底的绝佳选
择，因为它同时具备可执行性、可检查性和状态持久性。
And code, they argue, is uniquely suited to be the substrate of that harness,
because it is simultaneously executable, inspectable, and stateful.

11
00:01:33,454 --> 00:01:38,308
要理解为什么这很重要，想想之前的研究通常是如何使用代码的。
To understand why this matters, consider how prior work has typically used code.

12
00:01:39,118 --> 00:01:53,220
像「思维程序（思维程序）」或 PAL 这样的程序辅助推理方法意识到，
语言模型在算术和符号操作上不可靠，因此它们将计算任务委托给 Python 解释器。
Program-aided reasoning approaches like Program of Thoughts or PAL recognize that language models are unreliable at arithmetic and
symbolic manipulation, so they delegate computation to a Python interpreter.

13
00:01:53,550 --> 00:02:00,452
模型编写程序，解释器运行程序，答案便基于真实的执行结果返回。
The model writes a program, the interpreter runs it, and the answer comes back grounded in real execution.

14
00:02:00,846 --> 00:02:08,258
像 SACAN 或 CODAS 策略这样的具身智能体，将生成的程序作为机器人控制策略。
Embodied agents like SACAN or CODAS policies use generated programs as robot control policies.

15
00:02:08,654 --> 00:02:17,028
像 SWE bench 这样的软件工程基准测试，将仓库、测试和执行轨迹视为环境。
Software engineering benchmarks like SWE bench treat repositories, tests, and execution traces as the environment.

16
00:02:17,518 --> 00:02:23,360
这些每一个都是更广泛模式的一个切片，但该领域一直缺乏一个统一的框架。
Each of these is a slice of a broader pattern, but the field has lacked a unifying frame.

17
00:02:23,694 --> 00:02:29,348
作者通过将整个领域组织成三个相互关联的层级，提供了这个框架。
The authors offer that frame by organizing the entire landscape into three connected layers.

18
00:02:29,806 --> 00:02:35,396
第一层是智能体框架接口，这是代码首次进入智能体循环的地方。
The first layer is the harness interface, which is where code first enters the agent loop.

19
00:02:35,694 --> 00:02:37,760
在这里，代码扮演三个角色。
Here code plays three roles.

20
00:02:38,094 --> 00:02:47,460
它作为推理基底，将内部计算外部化为程序，以便解释器或形式验证器进行检查。
It serves as a reasoning substrate, externalizing internal computation into programs that interpreters or formal verifiers can check.

21
00:02:47,886 --> 00:02:55,620
你可以把它理解为在脑子里做算术与在纸上写下算式，让别人审计每一步的区别。
Think of this as the difference between doing arithmetic in your head versus writing it on paper where someone can audit each step.

22
00:02:56,110 --> 00:03:09,796
它作为行动接口，将高层意图转化为可执行的操作，无论是机器人运动指令、
基于 DOM 树的 GUI 点击，还是 API 调用。
It serves as an action interface, translating high-level intent into executable operations, whether that means robot motion commands,
GUI clicks grounded in DOM trees, or API calls.

23
00:03:10,318 --> 00:03:22,756
它还作为环境模型，其中仓库、模拟器、执行轨迹和
测试成为了智能体运行世界中持久的、可查询的表示。
And it serves as an environment model where repositories, simulators, execution traces, and tests become the persistent,
queryable representation of the world the agent operates in.

24
00:03:23,502 --> 00:03:26,756
关键的洞察是，这里的代码不是隐喻。
The crucial insight is that code is not metaphorical here.

25
00:03:27,150 --> 00:03:36,160
作者明确界定了这个术语，指代可执行或机器可检查的产物，
将其与原始感知或潜在的模型推理区分开来。
The authors explicitly bound the term to mean executable or machine checkable artifacts,
distinguishing it from raw perception or latent model reasoning.

26
00:03:36,366 --> 00:03:45,764
第二层是智能体框架机制，这是综述深入探讨如何
让智能体在长周期内保持可靠的操作机制的地方。
The second layer is harness mechanisms, and this is where the survey gets
into the operational machinery that keeps agents reliable over long horizons.

27
00:03:47,086 --> 00:03:54,880
规划被重新定义为智能体框架的控制问题，而非内部模型能力，它包含四种形式。
Planning is reframed not as an internal model capability, but as a harness control problem, with four flavors.

28
00:03:55,246 --> 00:03:59,920
线性分解，即智能体承诺执行一个单一的有序计划；
Linear decomposition, where the agent commits to a single ordered plan;

29
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:06,628
结构化规划，将决策锚定在依赖图或仓库结构中；
structure-grounded planning that anchors decisions in dependency graphs or repository structure;

30
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:14,080
基于搜索的规划，使用蒙特卡洛树搜索或类似技术探索多个轨迹；
search-based planning that explores multiple trajectories using Monte Carlo tree search or similar techniques;

31
00:04:14,382 --> 00:04:20,100
以及基于编排的规划，其中专门的角色通过分阶段的工作流进行协调。
and orchestration-based planning, where specialized roles coordinate through staged workflows.

32
00:04:20,622 --> 00:04:35,108
内存工程变成了一个状态管理层，它决定哪些内容留在活跃的上下文窗口中，
哪些内容被压缩成摘要，以及哪些内容被卸载到外部存储，比如向量数据库或文件系统产物。
Memory engineering becomes a state management layer that decides what stays in the active context window,
what gets compacted into summaries, and what gets offloaded to external storage like vector databases or file system artifacts.

33
00:04:35,726 --> 00:04:49,130
他们强调的一个巧妙做法是将 plan.md 或状态日志等 PLAN 文件视为持久化的框架对象，
支持版本控制和检查，这样智能体就能像软件工程师下班回家第二天早上再回来一样，
A clever recent practice they highlight is treating PLAN files like plan.md or status logs as persistent harness objects,
version controlled and inspectable, so that an agent can survive context resets the way

34
00:04:49,130 --> 00:04:51,520
他们强调的一个巧妙做法是将 plan.md 或状态日志等 PLAN 文件视为持久化的框架对象，
支持版本控制和检查，这样智能体就能像软件工程师下班回家第二天早上再回来一样，
a software engineer survives going home for the night and coming back the next morning.

35
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:54,660
在上下文重置后依然能继续工作。
a software engineer survives going home for the night and coming back the next morning.

36
00:04:55,150 --> 00:05:07,600
工具使用、规划、执行并针对确定性传感器进行验证的控制循环，
甚至通过遥测和进化智能体来实现框架的自我改进，全都存在这个层级中。
Tool use, control loops that plan, execute, and verify against deterministic sensors and even harness self-improvement through
telemetry and evolution agents all live in this layer.

37
00:05:07,918 --> 00:05:11,440
第三层将框架从单个智能体扩展到多个智能体。
The third layer scales the harness from one agent to many.

38
00:05:11,790 --> 00:05:26,980
当多个智能体在共享代码库上协作时，框架必须协调经理、规划者、代码编写者、
审查者和测试者等角色，支持从协作编程到对抗性红队测试的各种交互模式，
When multiple agents collaborate over a shared code base, the harness must coordinate roles like manager, planner, coder, reviewer,
and tester, support interaction modes from cooperative programming to adversarial red teaming, and arrange them in topologies,

39
00:05:26,980 --> 00:05:29,530
并将它们排列成从集中式到分布式再到流式传输的各种拓扑结构。
When multiple agents collaborate over a shared code base, the harness must coordinate roles like manager, planner, coder, reviewer,
and tester, support interaction modes from cooperative programming to adversarial red teaming, and arrange them in topologies,

40
00:05:29,530 --> 00:05:33,280
并将它们排列成从集中式到分布式再到流式传输的各种拓扑结构。
ranging from centralized to distributed to streaming.

41
00:05:33,678 --> 00:05:46,788
共享的代码产物、仓库、测试和执行轨迹成为了公共工作空间，
就像 Git 仓库作为人类工程团队的单一事实来源一样。
The shared code artifacts, repositories, tests, and execution traces become the common workspace,
much like how a Git repository serves as the source of truth for a human engineering team.

42
00:05:47,502 --> 00:05:56,004
这里的框架不再仅仅是围绕单个模型的运行时，而是许多模型达成共识的社会和技术架构。
The harness here is no longer just the runtime around one model, it's the
social and technical fabric through which many models reach consensus.

43
00:05:56,686 --> 00:06:02,948
作者随后调研了这种「代码即框架」的观点在不同应用领域中的体现。
The authors then survey how this code as harness view manifests across application domains.

44
00:06:03,438 --> 00:06:08,420
像 Claude Code 和 Codex 这样的编程助手，将仓库作为状态。
Coding assistants, like Claude Code and Codex, use repositories as state.

45
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:17,124
GUI 和操作系统智能体将操作锚定在 DOM 树和可访问性 API 中，并配备可执行的评估器。
GUI and OS agents ground actions in DOM trees and accessibility APIs with executable evaluators.

46
00:06:17,518 --> 00:06:24,720
科学发现智能体构建跨越模拟和实验室协议的假设测试流水线。
Scientific discovery agents compose hypothesis testing pipelines spanning simulations and lab protocols.

47
00:06:25,070 --> 00:06:29,840
像 Voyager 这样的具身智能体在 Minecraft 中构建持久的技能库。
Embodied agents like Voyager build persistent skill libraries in Minecraft.

48
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:34,400
个性化智能体维护可执行的用户配置文件。
Personalization agents maintain executable user profiles.

49
00:06:34,734 --> 00:06:35,920
这种模式不断重复。
The pattern repeats.

50
00:06:36,206 --> 00:06:40,004
代码提供了可检查、可执行的底层架构。
Code provides the inspectable, executable substrate.

51
00:06:40,430 --> 00:06:43,840
现在来看看调研中诚实反映出的局限性。
Now for the limitations, the survey honestly surfaces.

52
00:06:44,110 --> 00:06:52,000
评估是一个重大的开放问题，因为大多数基准测试衡量的是最终任务的成功，而不是框架的质量。
Evaluation is a significant open problem because most benchmarks measure final task success rather than harness quality.

53
00:06:52,398 --> 00:07:00,452
如果一个基准测试没有压力测试长程依赖管理，你就无
法判断规划的改进是真实的，还是测试设置产生的伪影。
If a benchmark doesn't stress long-range dependency management, you can't
tell whether planning improvements are real or artifacts of the test setup.

54
00:07:01,006 --> 00:07:08,160
在不完整反馈下的验证仍然很难，因为并非所有的失败都会产生清晰的运行时异常。
Verification under incomplete feedback remains hard, because not every failure produces a clean runtime exception.

55
00:07:08,494 --> 00:07:12,480
机器人伸手超过其工作空间时，可能只是静默失败。
A robot reaching past its workspace might just silently fail.

56
00:07:12,846 --> 00:07:21,120
无回归的框架改进是一个尚未解决的问题，因为进化框架本身可能会破坏之前正常工作的流程。
Regression-free harness improvement is an unsolved problem, since evolving
the harness itself risks breaking workflows that previously worked.

57
00:07:21,454 --> 00:07:27,040
多智能体系统在事务性共享状态和语义冲突解决方面面临困难。
Multi agent systems struggle with transactional shared state and semantic conflict resolution.

58
00:07:27,342 --> 00:07:35,040
这类似于经典的数据库一致性问题，但更难，因为冲突可能是语义上的，而非语法上的。
Similar to the classic database consistency problem, but harder, because the conflicts can be semantic rather than syntactic.

59
00:07:35,918 --> 00:07:47,428
此外，针对安全关键操作的人类监督、超越文本和代码的多模态扩展，
以及缺乏真正的框架工程科学，都仍是待开发的领域。
And human oversight for safety critical actions, multimodal extensions beyond text and code,
and the lack of a real science of harness engineering all remain open frontiers.

60
00:07:47,822 --> 00:07:51,792
现在让我们来看看在听完所有这些内容后，你可能会有的几个问题。
Now let's walk through some questions you might have after hearing all of this.

61
00:07:52,078 --> 00:07:57,152
首先，为什么代码作为框架媒介比自然语言更好？
First, why is code specifically better than natural language as a harness medium?

62
00:07:57,582 --> 00:08:00,644
答案归结为三个协同工作的属性。
The answer comes down to three properties that work together.

63
00:08:01,070 --> 00:08:10,500
可执行性意味着框架可以通过运行代码并观察实际后果来验证模型的意图，而不仅仅是转述它。
Executability means the harness can actually verify what the model intended
by running it and observing real consequences, not just paraphrasing it.

64
00:08:10,862 --> 00:08:18,500
可检查性意味着失败会产生轨迹和堆栈帧，框架可以读取这些信息并反馈到下一个推理步骤中。
Inspectability means failures produce traces and stack frames that the harness can read and feed back into the next reasoning step.

65
00:08:18,990 --> 00:08:28,112
而状态持久性意味着程序本身、仓库或执行日志在各
个步骤之间持久存在，这样智能体的进度就不会丢失。
And statefulness means the program itself, the repository, or the
execution log persists across steps so the agent's progress isn't lost.

66
00:08:28,526 --> 00:08:31,300
自然语言无法可靠地提供这些功能。
Natural language gives you none of these reliably.

67
00:08:31,598 --> 00:08:37,476
你可以用英语描述一个动作，但你没法运行它，没法对比它，也没法合并它。
You can describe an action in English, but you can't run it, you can't diff it, and you can't merge it.

68
00:08:37,902 --> 00:08:44,292
第二，把事物定义为智能体框架，而不是仅仅称之为智能体基础设施，究竟有什么新意？
Second, what's actually new about framing things as a harness rather than just calling it agent infrastructure?

69
00:08:44,878 --> 00:08:51,872
这种重新定义很重要，因为它把可靠性的核心从模型转移到了系统上。
The reframing matters because it shifts the locus of reliability away from the model and onto the system.

70
00:08:52,302 --> 00:09:03,712
如果你认为框架是瓶颈，你就会停止试图让模型变得更聪明，
转而尝试让周围的脚手架更稳健、更可检查、更易于恢复。
If you believe the harness is the bottleneck, you stop trying to make the model smarter and start trying to make the surrounding
scaffolding more robust, more inspectable, and more recoverable.

71
00:09:03,982 --> 00:09:06,832
它还统一了分散的研究方向。
It also unifies disparate research threads.

72
00:09:07,182 --> 00:09:23,556
程序辅助推理、机器人策略合成、仓库级编码智能体以及多智能体辩论框架，
最终都被证明是同一种底层模式的实例，这意味着一个领域的见解可以转移到另一个领域。
Program-aided reasoning, robot policy synthesis, repository-level coding agents, and multi-agent debate frameworks all turn out to be
instances of the same underlying pattern, which means insights from one domain can transfer to another.

73
00:09:24,206 --> 00:09:30,500
第三，动态生成的代码与人类设计的框架基础设施之间是什么关系？
Third, how does dynamically generated code relate to the human-designed harness infrastructure?

74
00:09:30,990 --> 00:09:33,952
这是综述中强调的一个微妙点。
This is a subtle point the survey emphasizes.

75
00:09:34,350 --> 00:09:44,672
智能体生成的代码，比如智能体为了检查数据库而编写的临时脚本，
或者它添加到库中的可重用技能，并不会取代更广泛的框架。
Agent-generated code, like a temporary script the agent writes to inspect a database
or a reusable skill it adds to its library, does not replace the broader harness.

76
00:09:45,294 --> 00:09:54,180
人类设计的层仍然掌控沙箱边界、权限层级、验证预言机以及人工审核关卡。
The human-designed layer still owns the sandbox boundaries, the
permission tiers, the verification oracles, and the human review gates.

77
00:09:54,512 --> 00:10:12,612
生成的代码让框架更具适应性，因为智能体可以围绕当前任务重塑其执行环境，
但围绕它的受政策管控的系统决定哪些代码可以被执行、信任或提升到未来的工作流中。
Generated code makes the harness more adaptive because the agent can reshape its execution environment around the current task,
but the policy-governed system around it decides what code may be executed, trusted, or promoted into future workflows.

78
00:10:13,326 --> 00:10:22,468
把智能体想象成一个可以在工作中制造工具的承包商，但建筑规范、
检查和许可证都是由其他人设定的。
Think of the agent as a contractor who can build tools on the job, but the
building code, the inspections, and the permits are set by someone else.

79
00:10:23,246 --> 00:10:30,404
现在，这些想法如何应用到服务于数亿用户的超大规模推荐系统中？
Now, how do these ideas land in the world of large-scale recommendation systems serving hundreds of millions of users?

80
00:10:30,862 --> 00:10:42,148
考虑到现代推荐系统正越来越多地转向智能体模式，
即语言模型负责编排检索、排序、解释和个性化。
Consider that modern recommenders are increasingly moving toward agentic patterns where
a language model orchestrates retrieval, ranking, explanation, and personalization.

81
00:10:42,734 --> 00:10:55,876
「代码即框架」的观点建议将用户状态、候选池、排序信号和政策约束视为可执行、
可检查的产物，而不是不透明的嵌入向量。
The code as harness view suggests treating user state, candidate pools, ranking signals, and policy constraints as executable,
inspectable artifacts rather than opaque embeddings.

82
00:10:56,526 --> 00:11:12,420
个性化智能体可以将用户的偏好模型维护为一个版本化的、可查询的程序，
